    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d140">

                <pb facs="0271" n="169" sameAs="frus:frus1933v01/pg169"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4/2003: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-05-27T11:00:00+01:00">May 27, 1933—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 27—6:43 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>666. If convenient I would appreciate your sending me by cable for my information
                    text of Japanese reply to the President’s message <pb facs="0272" n="170"
                        xml:id="pg170"/> of May 16th and résumé of any conversations you may have
                    had with Viscount Ishii with respect to disarmament matters.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
